Including file: StdAbout.pkg    (C:\Program Files\DataFlex 25.0\Pkg\StdAbout.pkg)
75107>>>// This provides a quick and simple way to create an about package for a program.
75107>>>// You need to create a message inside you client area called Activate_About.
75107>>>// Within this message you should send the message DoAbout passing needed
75107>>>// string information.
75107>>>//
75107>>>//       Procedure Activate_About
75107>>>//           Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor sBitmap
75107>>>//       End_Procedure
75107>>>//    where: sTitle =     Name of application. If none provided, uses caption
75107>>>//                        bar title
75107>>>//           sVersion   = Version Line. If none provided, will be blank
75107>>>//           sCopyRight = Copyright Line. If none provided, will be blank
75107>>>//           sAuthor    = Author name, blank if none provided
75107>>>//           sBitMap    = Bitmap logo. If none provided, standard VDF bitmap
75107>>>//                        is used.
75107>>>// It is expected that you will place this in your own object package. For
75107>>>// example an order about package may look like this:
75107>>>//
75107>>>//   // OrderAbout.pkg
75107>>>//   Use StdAbout.pkg
75107>>>//   Procedure Activate_About
75107>>>//      String sTitle sCopyright sVersion sAuthor
75107>>>//      Move "My Order Entry System" to sTitle
75107>>>//      Move "Version 2.1" to sVersion
75107>>>//      Move "Copyright xxxx, Super Software Inc." to sCopyright
75107>>>//      Move "John Smith"  to sAuthor
75107>>>//      Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor ""
75107>>>//   end_procedure
75107>>>//   // end of file.
75107>>>
